  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 133 AM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nThe upper high will slowly shift to the south and west through the \nend of the week. Strong subsidence from this feature will prevent \nany convection Friday and Saturday. The airmass over South-Central \nTexas remain about the same with low level flow from the east to \nsoutheast. Temperatures will will also be stagnant through the \nweekend. It will feel like an endless summer rather than the start \nof fall. By Sunday the upper high will have shifted far enough that \nisolated showers and thunderstorms will return during the afternoon \nand early evening. This pattern will repeat Monday. Tuesday models \nare showing the first real front of the season moving into TX. This \nwill bring chances for widespread rain Tuesday and Wednesday. The \nfront will move through our CWA Tuesday night and early Wednesday. \nNortherly to northeasterly winds behind the front will bring cooler, \ndrier air. Highs Wednesday will be in the 80s in the Hill Country \nand Southern Edwards Plateau and near 90 in the I-35 Corridor and \nCoastal Plains.",
